sequenceDiagram
    participant App as App<br>[implements GapCentralResponse]
    participant Node as Node<br>[implements GapCentral]

    App->>Node: GapCentral.SetDeviceDiscoveryFilter(<br>filter=address, data=C4:AB:12:34:56:78)
    App->>Node: GapCentral.StartDeviceDiscovery()
    Node-->>App: GapCentralResponse.CurrentState(scanning)

    Note over App, Node: No matching devices found. DeviceDiscovered is never received.

    alt App-managed timeout
        Note over App: App-side timeout expires (e.g. 10 s).
        App->>Node: GapCentral.Standby()
        Node-->>App: GapCentralResponse.CurrentState(standby)
    else Stack-managed timeout (stack-dependent)
        Note over Node: Some BLE stacks auto-terminate<br>the discovery procedure after<br>a stack-defined maximum.
        Node-->>App: GapCentralResponse.CurrentState(standby)
        Note over App: App receives an unsolicited CurrentState(standby).<br>The App must handle this without a matching Standby() call.
    end

    Note over App, Node: GapCentral does not expose a scan timeout in its API.<br>The App is responsible for its own scan-timeout policy.<br>Whether the underlying stack additionally imposes<br>its own maximum is stack-dependent.
